==Strategy==
If one owns [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], this stage becomes almost trivial. Just send him with support from [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] and [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] and the peons or [[Queen B]] won't stand a chance. Nevertheless, it's easy to lose in this stage because of [[Brollow|the]] [[Kroxo|peons]] getting in the way. Try to keep your defenses tight and spam to keep your base safe. [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Onmyoji Cat]] can potentially help against [[THE SLOTH]].

[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] all decently help in this stage, between Catellite having [[Immune to Slow|Slow Immunity]], Castaway Cat having a chance to [[Freeze|freeze]] Queen B, while also having decent speed and a chance to survive a lethal strike and Dancing Flasher Cat having exceptional stats. Dancing Flasher Cat's [[True Form]] can also improve in speed via [[Talents]], which help in timing them. '''DON'T BRING ANY ATTACKER WITH LESS THAN 9 SPEED''', as they'll do nothing save for draining cash.

===Recommended Ubers===
Generally, any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] that moves fast, is easily replaceable or has a [[Special Abilities|special ability]] against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] or [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies should do well, below this will have more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[Strike Unit R.E.I. (Uber Rare Cat)|Strike Unit R.E.I.]]: Just like [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]] in [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]], R.E.I. is a designated "counter" against Queen B. Her immunity to Slow and Massive Damage to Floating allows her to come on in and bash the bug's head into oblivion. Just be sure to clear the path and be careful of THE SLOTH, as she can't take a lot of hits.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Divine Kai μ's relativity quick speed allows her to get in the Queen's blind spot easily, and even if she gets hit she has so much health that she might be able to get to the blind spot without dying. Her extremely damaging hits and already-high HP also gives her the ability to get rid of THE SLOTH as well as keep the Brollows at bay.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Greater Balrog's insane DPS is something to never underestimate, and with an enemy with a large blind spot, he becomes one of the most powerful units you can have. While you might need to time his deployment to ensure he doesn't get hit, his low cooldown gives you many attempts for him to get in and start clobbering.
*[[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]]: Extremely fast, with low cost and short recharge time for an Uber. Has enough range to stay out of trouble most of the time, and has a very fast attack rate which is useful for destroying Brollows and Kroxos. Just make sure that you don't send them out right before Queen B attacks or they will easily die, otherwise, they will serve you well.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: Similar to Greater Balrog Cat, Cats in the Cradle have less offense, but much better defense and tanking capabilities. They have enough health to tank SLOTH attacks, and their crippling [[Wave Attack]] can easily take out the Brollows and Kroxos. They also have enough health to tank Queen B's attacks and make a sort of wall, and their recharge and cost makes them very disposable.
*[[Blanka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blanka CC]]: Being an anti-Alien [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]], Blanka absolutely crushes this stage. Having the attack power of Awakened Bahamut against Aliens, and the health to tank Brollow and THE SLOTH's attacks, he combined with Butterfly Cat can make Honey Trap almost a walk in the park.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]]: Trivializes this stage with her abilities and tankiness, allowing you to focus your lineup more towards the continuation stage.

